alamo.program = lagrangian_shock_cp_damage
alamo.program.mechanics.model = finite.crystalplastic

# ============================================================================
# PRODUCTION DECK — 1024 x 256, well-resolved phase field (ell/dx = 4.75)
#   dx = 0.003504/1024 = 3.421875e-6
#   dy = 0.00052/256   = 2.031250e-6   (aspect dx/dy = 1.68)
#   ell = 1.625e-5 held FIXED -> ell/dx = 4.75, ell/dy = 8.0  (>= 2 satisfied)
#   Gc  = 1.083333e4 held FIXED -> Gc/ell = 6.667e8  => spall strength unchanged
#       sigma_c = sqrt(3 E Gc / 8 ell) invariant vs coarser ladder rungs.
#   dt is CAP-limited (timestep = 1e-10 < CFL limit ~3e-10 at this dx),
#       so step count ~= coarse mesh; cost multiplier ~= cell count only (~32x).
#   CAVEAT: node-stored CP state / cell-read stress (amr.node.all = 1) still
#       carries the 2*dx collocation mode. Refining relocates it to shorter
#       wavelength; it does NOT remove it. Convergence/PCC claims off this run
#       remain gated on the cell-centered FabArray<BaseFab<MODEL>> refactor.
# ============================================================================

